## The suite (built — 6 profiles)

All share: either codec incl. AV1 (un-banned), Remux/Full Disc banned except where noted,
`Banned Groups` kept (the upstream-synced junk list), and the **DV rule** (all profiles):
`Dolby Vision (Without Fallback)` excluded, `Dolby Vision` with fallback wanted, HDR a bonus.

| Profile | Op | Shape |
|---|---|---|
| **1080p Main** | 213 | 1080p-only. WEB-DL 860k (small-file default) > trusted Bluray ~300k > unknown Bluray 40k > WEBRip 25k. Floor 20k. |
| **2160p Main** | 217 | 2160p-only. 2160p WEB-DL 920k > trusted UHD Bluray ~300k > unknown UHD Bluray 40k. SDR allowed (0), HDR bonus. Floor 20k. |
| **2160p Preferred** | 221 | 2160p high / 1080p fallback. 2160p WEB-DL 920k, trusted UHD BR ~490k; 1080p WEB-DL 400k ("great 1080p") beats unknown 4K BR 40k ("crappy 4K"). No WEBRip. Floor 20k. |
| **1080p Preferred** | 224 | Mirror: 1080p high (860k) / 2160p fallback (400k). Great 4K beats crappy 1080p. No WEBRip. Floor 20k. |
| **Archive** | 226 | Remux-first, 8-tier: trusted 2160p Remux 980k > trusted UHD BR 850k > any 2160p Remux 800k > any UHD BR 750k > trusted 1080p Remux 430k > trusted 1080p BR 400k > any 1080p Remux 250k > any 1080p BR 200k. **Floor 150k** (rejects WEB-DL/junk). WEB-DL weights dropped as belt-and-suspenders. |
| **Any** | 228 | Permissive catch-all. Strict resolution ladder (2160p 920-960k > 1080p 680-760k > 720p 500-560k > 480/576 340-380k > DVD 200k > SDTV 100k), group tiers flattened, all bans lifted except guardrails. **Floor 1.** |

**Audio / channel / vendor model (op 229, all profiles):** channel CFs `7.1 Surround` (+3000)
and `5.1 Surround` (+2000) were created (from the existing 5.1/7.1 regex) and dominate; codec
ladder (lossless ~800–1600 → lossy ~100–600) is secondary; streaming vendors (`AMZN`/`DSNP`/
`ATVP`/`HMAX`/`MAX`/`iT`/`NF`/`MA`) dropped to a flat **50** tiebreaker. Priority within a
source: **channels ≫ lossless codec > vendor**. (Audio scores are all far below source
weights, so audio never overrides resolution.) Note: audio CFs are otherwise codec-based — a
codec CF can't tell 5.1 from 2.0, which is why the channel CFs were needed.

